            "text": "Millings themselves do not turn to mud the way soil does, but a driveway can still get soft and rutted if water saturates a poor base underneath. Muddy spots in a millings driveway almost always point to a drainage or base problem. Fix the crown and drainage, then patch with fresh millings and compact them."
